      "raw": "<p>I haven&#39;t seen a offical admin post on this yet. Maybe I didn&#39;t go deep enough into the ones that had 50 pages.</p><p>But first the wording of Wrest the Mind:<br />&nbsp;</p><p>Play this card next to a Target, other than a Hero or Villain Character Card. Whenever that target deals damage,<strong> you may</strong> redirect that damage to another target. <strong>If you do</strong>, <strong>The Visionary</strong> deals 3 psychic damage to that target and 3 psychic damage to <strong>herself</strong>.</p><p>If the target leaves play, destroy this card.</p><p>I bolded a few key words:</p><p>&quot;you may,&quot; so you don&#39;t have too.</p><p>&quot;If you do,&quot; Conditional reaction.</p><p>&quot;The Visionary&quot; &amp; &quot;herself&quot;</p><p>Basically the general arguement is does she take the damage if redirects and kills the target thus removing the card. I think the best way to view this is the order of operations.</p><p>Target: Electro-Pulse Bomb (Omintron device: 15HP).</p><p>Start of Villain turn. EPB does 15 damage to 4 heros.</p><p>Wrest the Mind is used to Redirect 15 damage to EPB<br />Conditional Reaction is activate:<br />15 damage to EPB<br />3 Damage to EPB<br />3 Damage to Visionary.<br />But there are two interupts. So the Order would be</p><p>15 Damage to EPB<br />Destroy EPB<br />Destroy Wrest the Mind<br />3 Damage to EPB (From The Visionary not the card as the card doesn&#39;t do the damage and The Visionary is still in play, also it is a Conditional Reaction so it happens because she did the action) Damage is ignored as the target is destroyed.<br />3 Damage to Visionary (as she is still in play and the damage is from a Conditional Reaction of her, and not damage from the card).</p><p>If I could get a Admin/Game designer to verify if this is correct that would be nice.<br />&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
